{"id": 8356980, "full_name": "Brian T. Emmer", "first_name": "Brian T.", "last_name": "Emmer", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}], "custom_fields": [], "figshare_url": "https://plos.figshare.com/articles/figure/Comparison_of_CRISPR_screen_results_for_modifiers_of_HuH7_LDL_endocytosis_HuH7_5_SARS-CoV-2_infection_and_HuH7_ACE2_surface_abundance_/19287245", "download_disabled": false, "description": "<p>(A) The subset of genes tested by high-resolution CRISPR screening for both LDL endocytosis and ACE2 surface abundance were divided into those whose disruption reduced LDL uptake (n = 15) and \u201cother genes\u201d whose disruption did not reduce LDL uptake (n = 55). The Z-score for each gene within each group was then compared for each of the viral CPE screens reported by Schneider et al. Asterisks indicate p < 0.05 by Student\u2019s t-test. (B) Genes were grouped as in (A) and compared for their association with surface ACE2 abundance in secondary screens of either HuH7 wild-type or ACE2-enriched cells. (C) Heat maps for log-transformed p-values of canonical SREBP regulators <i>LDLR</i>, <i>SCAP</i>, <i>MBTPS1</i>, and <i>MBTPS2</i> in screens of HuH7 LDL uptake [<a href=\"http://www.plospathogens.org/article/info:doi/10.1371/journal.ppat.1010377#ppat.1010377.ref043\" target=\"_blank\">43</a>] and ACE2 surface abundance (this study) and HuH7.5 SARS-CoV-2 cytopathic effect [<a href=\"http://www.plospathogens.org/article/info:doi/10.1371/journal.ppat.1010377#ppat.1010377.ref035\" target=\"_blank\">35</a>].</p> <p>(TIF)</p>", "funding": null, "funding_list": [], "version": 1, "status": "public", "size": 661294, "created_date": "2022-03-01T18:39:36Z", "modified_date": "2023-06-15T00:46:41Z", "is_public": true, "is_confidential": false, "is_metadata_record": false, "confidential_reason": "", "metadata_reason": "", "license": {"value": 1, "name": "CC BY 4.0", "url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"}, "tags": ["viral spike protein", "throughput crispr screens", "suggest potential targets", "influence cellular susceptibility", "immortalized cell lines", "established transcription factors", "cell type specificity", "3 cells revealed", "host factors involved", "derived huh7 cells", "div >< p", "ace2 regulatory networks", "ace2 modifiers comprised", "ace2 surface abundance", "host cells", "surface abundance", "functional networks", "functional modifiers", "derived calu", "regulate ace2", "ace2 regulators", "ace2 expression", "ace2 </", "vivo </", "ugp2 </", "smad4 </", "report high", "pias1 </", "orthogonal screening", "mrna level", "molecular pathways", "mogs </", "kdm6a </", "gpaa1 </", "findings clarify", "epigenetic regulators", "ep300 </", "enriched among", "distinct set", "bambi </", "2 infection", "2 entry"], "keywords": ["viral spike protein", "throughput crispr screens", "suggest potential targets", "influence cellular susceptibility", "immortalized cell lines", "established transcription factors", "cell type specificity", "3 cells revealed", "host factors involved", "derived huh7 cells", "div >< p", "ace2 regulatory networks", "ace2 modifiers comprised", "ace2 surface abundance", "host cells", "surface abundance", "functional networks", "functional modifiers", "derived calu", "regulate ace2", "ace2 regulators", "ace2 expression", "ace2 </", "vivo </", "ugp2 </", "smad4 </", "report high", "pias1 </", "orthogonal screening", "mrna level", "molecular pathways", "mogs </", "kdm6a </", "gpaa1 </", "findings clarify", "epigenetic regulators", "ep300 </", "enriched among", "distinct set", "bambi </", "2 infection", "2 entry"], "categories": [{"id": 4, "title": "Biochemistry", "parent_id": 38, "path": "", "source_id": "", "taxonomy_id": 10}, {"id": 7, "title": "Medicine", "parent_id": 48, "path": "", "source_id": "", "taxonomy_id": 10}, {"id": 8, "title": "Microbiology", "parent_id": 48, "path": "", "source_id": "", "taxonomy_id": 10}, {"id": 12, "title": "Cell Biology", "parent_id": 48, "path": "", "so